{"duration_api_ms":9104,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"032ffbd7-61af-40f9-948e-3fcd86a8c7d4","total_cost_usd":0.0262145,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1054,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":880,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":519},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1054,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":880,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1054,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1054},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1620,"outputTokens":25,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0001745,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":880,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1054,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.02604,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":519,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":1054,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Written basket policies (Rule 6c-11(c)(3))**\n- Funds must adopt written policies and procedures on basket construction and acceptance.\n- Custom-basket policies must also:\n  - set detailed construction and acceptance parameters in the best interests of the fund and shareholders;\n  - include a process for revising or deviating from them;\n  - name the titles or roles of staff reviewing each custom basket for compliance.\n\n**Records (Rule 6c-11(d))**, kept five years (first two easily accessible):\n- authorized participant (AP) agreements;\n- for each basket exchanged: each holding's name, quantity and identifier (ticker, CUSIP, etc.), any cash, whether custom, and a statement of policy compliance.\n\n**Custom basket vs. non-standard order**\n- A **custom basket** turns on composition: not a pro-rata portfolio slice (beyond permitted adjustments), or differing from other baskets that day.\n- A **non-standard order**, not a rule term, is an operational variation (size, cut-off, fees, settlement). It is custom only if composition changes.","ttft_ms":6103,"type":"result","duration_ms":8606,"uuid":"05605033-c4d8-4d82-9908-66bfcccb4a4f","ttft_stream_ms":1476,"time_to_request_ms":70,"first_content_frame_ms":1476,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
